  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef ml_feature_scaling(X: list, method: str = 'standard') -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Feature Scaling** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef ml_feature_scaling(X: list, method: str = 'standard') -> list:\n    arr = np.array(X, dtype=float)\n    if method == 'standard':\n        s = np.std(arr, axis=0)\n        return np.round(np.where(s > 1e-12, (arr - np.mean(arr, axis=0)) / s, 0.0), 4).tolist()\n    diff = np.max(arr, axis=0) - np.min(arr, axis=0)\n    return np.round(np.where(diff > 1e-12, (arr - np.min(arr, axis=0)) / diff, 0.0), 4).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
